Clearly, we do NOT want to be deluged with posts from critics--this
list is not meant to serve as a forum where Extropians defend their
world-view against all counter arguments that the ingenuity of the
non-extropians can devise--as Tom has already pointed out.  But neither
should we be so insular that we appear to others to have closed minds
and closed ears.

I thought Tom's initial reaction to what appeared to be a post from the
White House was too extreme.  But I agree that this is an Extropian
forum where Extropianism should be taken for granted, and outsiders are
guests whose welcome depends on their courteous behavior.

We have every right to reject whatever posts we object to, but that is
not the issue.  The issue is whether utter rejection out of hand of all
White House posts (for example) would best serve our interests.  I
posit that it would not.


--alan (lovejoy@alc.com)


